+# UC13 Delete profile design
+
+Intent: implement issue14 / UC13 FR-PR05/06, BR03/04/20/23 and all AF01–05 in the authorized batch. Owner recoverably trashes one active own profile and receives a durable operation identifier and exact30-day UTC expiry. New durable lifecycle metadata warrants written design/plan. Independent approvals remain development-only deferred; no release gate changes.
+
+DELETE /api/profiles/{id}, canonical nonzero lowercaseD public GUID, current identity bearer and one vault-access header. Strict bounded UTF8 JSON containing only expectedRevision, no query/unknown/duplicate/numeric-string fields. Expected revision comes from the common online-write concurrency contract. Success200 metadata6fields: profileId,trashOperationId,revision,serverSequence,deletedAt,purgeAt. No ciphertext or keys; all responses no-store. Invalidinput400; hidden/absent/trashed/terminal targets404; missingidentity/access401, invalidcurrentaccount/session/scope403 (absent/closing/erasedaccount404); stale visible revision or counter exhaustion409; dependency503 with rollback.
+
+Preferred dedicated transactional store follows account→session→profile locks like UC12. Recheck current statement time AFTER profile lock before revision decisions, then final atomic UPDATE repeats account/session/current policy/visibility/expectedrevision and statement_timestamp expiry checks. Alternative single-table metadata-only trash cannot cleanly retain future same-operation cascades; an immediate purge contradicts recoverability and needs the separate erasure workflow. No irreversible purge here.
+
+Only selected own profile or account-wide access permits deletion. Store increments profile revision/globalsequence, retains client EditedAt and opaque content/wrappers/ownership, sets deletedAt at final database statement and purgeAt exactly720hours later (UTC30days independent of timezone/DST). Corrupt counters fail503; sequence/revision exhaustion409, no partial mutation. Metadata fetched/validated before commit. Revoke ALL owned sessions selected to this profile atomically, preserving accountwide/unrelated scopes; restoration must never revive pretrash handles. Reads/lists already exclude trashed profiles.
+
+Durable schema: TrashOperation(internalId,unique PublicId,AccountId FK,RootResourceKind/RootResourceId,DeletedAt,PurgeAt); TrashEntry(internalId,OperationId FK,ResourceKind/ResourceId,required AssociationSnapshot bytes), unique current typedresource, operation membership cascades with operation metadata. Distinct operation/group membership supports later folder cascades and restore of only entities this operation deleted. For this actual domain: one profile entry, typed snapshot of3actualempty ID arrays; no record/folder/collection/link entities exist. Creation rejects nonempty links; first entity/sharing UCs must extend actual deactivation/snapshot/preservation tests before their flows release. No fake resource entities or claimed nonempty preservation evidence.
+
+Enqueue RetentionWorkItem(OperationKey=trash/{operation-guid},DueAt=purgeAt) in the same transaction. Existing worker fails closed for unregistered typed handlers; UC53 supplies actual trash purge, UC50/51/52 supply list/restore/explicit purge. Expired entries are inaccessible immediately even if physical cleanup retries. Before any physical erasure releases, resolve persistent global ResourceId-only cross-kind tombstone collisions and integrate typed handler/restore reconciliation. Keep durable due work; never mark it completed without a handler. This dependency is explicit, not a claim that purge exists now. UC39 complete rotation continues including retained trashed profile bytes; signed wrapper revision can precede newer trash revision.
+
+Concurrency: visible edit winning first makes stale trash409; trash winning first makes later edit404. Concurrent delete/lost-response retry after committed trash returns404 without duplicate operation or extendeddeadline. Every failure rolls back profile/session/trash/queue writes; same original request can retry after rollback. Cancellation propagates.
+
+Current CONTRIBUTING now requires Unreleased changelog entries. Update UC13 change in thisPR and catch up UC12 entry because parallel owner docsPR72 introduced that policy while UC12 was in flight; cannot retroactively amend mergedPR73. Preserve all owner docs. No repeated approval menus under existing batch authorization. Future merge orchestration must stop on failed local readiness and require fresh exacthead/MERGEABLE/CLEAN/all latestchecksSUCCESS before normal matchhead merge.
+
+Verification: native realprofile fixtures, actualPG schema/constraints/atomicstate/concurrency/expiry/rollback/queue, command failclosed output, actualHTTP/Heimdall strictboundaries/visibility/sessionrevocation/no-store. Fullunfiltered0fail/0skip >=90%productionline, reportbranch; helper/spec/OpenAPI/diff; one ordinary finalreview and one TDD correctionpass if blockers; requiredCI normalmerge/issueDone/archive thenUC14. Selfcheck all FR/BR/AF exist, no placeholders; recovery dependencies explicitly assigned.
